{{also|Mine|miné|minè|minę|míně|-mine}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|mīn}}, {{IPA|en|/maɪ̯n/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-mine.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪn|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|min}}, {{m|enm|myn}}, from {{inh|en|ang|mīn}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*mīn}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*mīnaz}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*méynos}}.

Cognate with {{cog|stq|mien}}, {{cog|fy|myn}}, {{cog|nl|mijn}}, {{cog|nds|mien}}, {{cog|de|mein}}, {{cog|da|-}}, {{cog|sv|-}} and {{cog|no|min}}, {{cog|is|mín}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|en|myne||obsolete}}

====Pronoun====
{{head|en|pronoun|cat2=possessive pronouns|cat3=first person pronouns}}

# That which belongs to me.
## {{non-gloss definition|Used predicatively.}}
##: {{ux|en|The house itself is '''mine''', but the land is not.}}
## {{non-gloss definition|Used substantively, with an implied noun.}}
##: {{ux|en|'''Mine''' has been a long journey.}}
## {{non-gloss definition|Used absolutely, set off from the sentence.}}
##: {{ux|en|'''Mine''' for only a week so far, it already feels like an old friend.}}
## {{non-gloss definition|Used otherwise not directly before the possessed noun.}} {{rfex|en}}

